S1: Train the Models In your first terminal, navigate to your project directory and run all three training scripts.
        python train_model_alzheimers.py
        python train_model_braintumor.py
        python train_model_parkinsons.py
S2: Run the Backend API Open a new terminal (do not close the first one yet, just in case). 
    Go to the same project directory (of app.py) and run the Flask application using the command `python app.py` on that new terminal. Keep this terminal running.
    It's now running your server on http://127.0.0.1:5000 and http://10.116.255.100:5000 open both and keep them open.
S3: Run the Frontend Server In your VSCode file explorer:
    Right-click on your "frontend" folder.
    Select "Open in Integrated Terminal".
    In the new terminal that opens (which is already in the frontend directory), run the following command " python -m http.server 8000 ". Keep this terminal running.
S4: Use the Application
    Open your web browser (like Chrome or Firefox).
    Go to this address: http://localhost:8000
